### Configuration Files

#### `terra.tf` (Provider & Backend Settings)

Configures the required provider versions and targets the AWS region.

```hcl
[ec2-user@ip-172-31-3-89 ~]$ cat terra.tf 
terraform {
  required_providers {

    aws = {
      source  = "hashicorp/aws"
      version = ">= 6.42.0"
    }

    random = {
      source  = "hashicorp/random"
      version = "3.8.1"
    }

  }
}

provider "aws" {
  region = "ap-south-1"
  alias  = "ubuntu_IND"
}

```

#### `network_resource.tf` (Networking Layer)

Defines an AWS VPC and a subnet dependent on that VPC's ID, complete with custom descriptive tags.

```hcl
[ec2-user@ip-172-31-3-89 ~]$ cat network_resource.tf 
resource "aws_vpc" "my_vpc" {
  cidr_block = "10.0.0.0/16"

  tags = {
    Name = "My-jhakash-taint-vpc"
  }
}

resource "aws_subnet" "my_subnet" {
  vpc_id     = aws_vpc.my_vpc.id
  cidr_block = "10.0.0.0/24"

  tags = {
    Name = "my-jhakash-taint-subnet"
  }
}

```

#### `resour.tf` (Storage & Security Layer)

Defines an S3 bucket alongside an attached public access block configuration referencing the bucket's name.

```hcl
[ec2-user@ip-172-31-3-89 ~]$ cat resour.tf 
resource "aws_s3_bucket" "my_s3" {
  bucket = "my-jhakash-taint-bucket"
}

resource "aws_s3_bucket_public_access_block" "from_tainted" {
  bucket = aws_s3_bucket.my_s3.bucket

  block_public_acls       = false
  block_public_policy     = false
  ignore_public_acls      = true
  restrict_public_buckets = true
}

```

